---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = "Refund Policy — My4MLife";
const description = "My4MLife refund, cancellation, and return policy for subscriptions, consults, supplements, and prescription medications.";
const canonical = "https://www.my4mlife.com/refund-policy";
const ogImage = "https://www.my4mlife.com/og-image.svg";
const robots = "index, follow";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogImage={ogImage} robots={robots}>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="page-crumb">LEGAL</span>
    <h1>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>
    <p>How refunds, cancellations, and returns work across My4MLife products and services.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content">
  <div class="container legal-container">

    <div class="meta-dates">
      <strong>Effective Date:</strong> 2026-05-18<br/>
      <strong>Last Updated:</strong> 2026-05-18
    </div>

    <p class="lede">My4MLife is a health-education and protocol-coaching platform. Medical care, prescriptions, and lab orders are provided by our contracted licensed telemedicine partner. The policies below apply to charges billed by My4MLife. Where the medical partner bills separately, their own refund policy governs that portion.</p>

    <h2>Subscription cancellation</h2>
    <p>You may cancel any My4MLife subscription at any time through your account dashboard or by emailing <a href="mailto:refunds@my4mlife.com">refunds@my4mlife.com</a>. Cancellation stops the next billing cycle. We do not pro-rate or refund the current billing period after it has begun, except as described under "Seven-day cancellation window" below.</p>

    <h2>Seven-day cancellation window (subscriptions only)</h2>
    <p>If you cancel a NEW subscription within seven (7) days of your first charge, we will refund that first month in full — provided no consult has been completed and no prescription medications have shipped. This is a buyer's-remorse window for first-time subscribers.</p>

    <h2>Completed consults — non-refundable</h2>
    <p>Fees for completed telemedicine consults are not refundable. Your fee covers the clinician's time and the protocol delivered. If you scheduled a consult and did not attend without rescheduling at least 24 hours in advance, the consult is treated as completed for refund purposes (the clinician's time was reserved for you).</p>

    <h2>Cancelled (unstarted) consults — full refund</h2>
    <p>If you cancel a consult more than 24 hours before the scheduled time, we issue a full refund within 5–7 business days. If you reschedule (rather than cancel), no refund is issued — your payment carries over to the new appointment.</p>

    <h2>Prescription medications — non-refundable once shipped</h2>
    <p>Federal and state pharmacy regulations prohibit the return or resale of dispensed prescription medications once they have left the pharmacy. Once your medication has shipped, the charge for that order is final, regardless of whether the package has been delivered.</p>
    <p>If your order has not yet shipped, you may cancel for a full refund by contacting <a href="mailto:refunds@my4mlife.com">refunds@my4mlife.com</a> as soon as possible. We will attempt to halt the shipment; we cannot guarantee success if cancellation is requested close to ship time.</p>

    <h2>Supplements and nutraceuticals — case-by-case</h2>
    <p>Unopened, unused supplements may be returned within 14 days of delivery for a refund minus shipping and a restocking fee. Opened products are non-refundable. Damaged or defective products will be replaced at no charge — contact us with a photo.</p>

    <h2>App access</h2>
    <p>Access to the My4MLife app is tied to your active subscription status. When your subscription ends, app access ends with it. There is no separate refund for app access; it is included with your purchased products and services.</p>

    <h2>No-show, missed, or late-arrival consults</h2>
    <p>If you miss a scheduled consult or arrive more than 15 minutes late without prior notice, the consult is treated as completed for refund purposes. The clinician's time was reserved and cannot be reclaimed. You may reschedule a future consult, but the original fee is not refunded or credited.</p>

    <h2>Lab orders</h2>
    <p>Lab fees are non-refundable once the lab requisition has been generated by the clinician. If you choose not to complete a lab draw after the requisition is issued, the fee is forfeit. Lab work performed by Quest, Labcorp, or any third-party lab is subject to that lab's own billing and refund policies, which may apply in addition to ours.</p>

    <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Email <a href="mailto:refunds@my4mlife.com">refunds@my4mlife.com</a> from the address on your My4MLife account.</li>
      <li>Include your order number or the email used at checkout.</li>
      <li>Describe what you're asking us to refund and why.</li>
      <li>We respond within 3 business days. Approved refunds are processed within 5–7 business days back to the original payment method.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Chargebacks</h2>
    <p>If you have a billing dispute, please contact us before initiating a chargeback with your card issuer. Chargebacks are time-consuming for both parties and may result in account suspension while the dispute resolves. We will always work in good faith to resolve a legitimate billing issue directly.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Refund Policy from time to time. Material changes will be communicated by email to active subscribers at least 30 days in advance. The "Last Updated" date at the top reflects when this policy was most recently revised.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Refund and billing questions:</strong> <a href="mailto:refunds@my4mlife.com">refunds@my4mlife.com</a><br/>
      <strong>General support:</strong> <a href="mailto:hello@my4mlife.com">hello@my4mlife.com</a>
    </p>

    <p class="legal-footer-links">
      Related: <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
    </p>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
.page-crumb {
  display: inline-block;
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  color: var(--accent);
  background: rgba(0,184,148,0.15);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0,184,148,0.35);
  padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
}
.legal-container { max-width: 780px; }
.meta-dates {
  font-size: 0.88rem;
  color: var(--text-light);
  padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
  background: var(--bg-soft);
  border-radius: 8px;
  margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
}
.lede {
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  line-height: 1.65;
  padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
  background: rgba(0,184,148,0.06);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  border-radius: 8px;
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
}
.legal-container h2 {
  font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
  font-size: 1.3rem;
  color: var(--primary);
  margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
}
.legal-container p { line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
.legal-container ol, .legal-container ul { line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text); padding-left: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
.legal-container li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
.legal-footer-links {
  margin-top: 2.5rem;
  padding-top: 1.2rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  font-size: 0.92rem;
  color: var(--text-light);
}
.legal-footer-links a { color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline; }
</style>

</BaseLayout>
